---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SEO from '../components/SEO.astro';
import AdSense from '../components/AdSense.astro';
import DataStorageConverter from '../components/tools/DataStorageConverter';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <SEO slot="head" title="Data Storage Converter" description="Convert between bytes, KB, MB, GB, TB, and PB data storage units." />
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How many MB are in a GB?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"One gigabyte equals 1,000 megabytes (decimal) or 1,024 mebibytes (binary).\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Why does my drive show less space?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Drive manufacturers use decimal (1 GB = 1,000 MB) while operating systems use binary (1 GiB = 1,024 MiB), so a 500 GB drive shows about 465 GiB.\"}}]}"} />

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-primary-600">Home</a> <span class="mx-2">›</span> <span class="text-gray-900">Data Storage Converter</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Data Storage Converter</h1>

    <DataStorageConverter client:load />

    <AdSense slot="middle" />

    <div class="mt-12 prose prose-gray max-w-none">
      <h2>How to Convert Data Storage Units</h2><p>Data storage conversion is essential in computing. Understanding the difference between decimal (KB, MB, GB) and binary (KiB, MiB, GiB) units helps avoid confusion when buying storage devices.</p><h3>Decimal vs Binary</h3><p>In decimal: 1 KB = 1,000 bytes. In binary: 1 KiB = 1,024 bytes. This is why a "500 GB" hard drive shows less space in your operating system.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="border-b border-gray-100 pb-4 last:border-0">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How many MB are in a GB?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-600">One gigabyte equals 1,000 megabytes (decimal) or 1,024 mebibytes (binary).</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-b border-gray-100 pb-4 last:border-0">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Why does my drive show less space?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-600">Drive manufacturers use decimal (1 GB = 1,000 MB) while operating systems use binary (1 GiB = 1,024 MiB), so a 500 GB drive shows about 465 GiB.</p>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <AdSense slot="bottom" />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
